{"kind":"symbol","schemaVersion":{"patch":0,"minor":3,"major":0},"sections":[],"hierarchy":{"paths":[[]]},"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/ChoosingASearchTree","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/TriesAndSuffixStructures","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/DecisionDiagrams","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/RangeAndSpatialTrees","doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph"],"title":"Guides","anchor":"Guides"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"content":[{"anchor":"Overview","level":2,"type":"heading","text":"Overview"},{"inlineContent":[{"code":"import GrafluentCollections","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" imports every module. Each module also has its own documentation","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"and can be imported on its own.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["import GrafluentCollections","","var scores: FenwickTree = [3, 1, 4, 1, 5, 9, 2, 6]","print(scores.prefixSum(through: 3))  \/\/ 9","print(scores.sum(in: 2 ..< 6))       \/\/ 19"]},{"anchor":"Values-not-references","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Values, not references"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Every collection is a copy-on-write struct. Assigning one copies nothing until one of the copies"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"is mutated; then only that copy pays, once, and the other keeps its elements:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let original: BTree = [1, 2, 3]","var copy = original","copy.insert(4)","Array(original)   \/\/ [1, 2, 3]","Array(copy)       \/\/ [1, 2, 3, 4]"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"The vertices of a tree live in flat arrays linked by integer indices rather than in a class per","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"vertex, so a copy is a few array copies and a traversal reads memory almost in order. The API","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"follows the standard library and Swift Collections: the sorted sets are ","type":"text"},{"code":"SetAlgebra","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" and","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"random-access collections indexed by rank, the dictionaries take ","type":"text"},{"code":"subscript(_:default:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", and the","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"range trees are collections of their values.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Traps-and-checked-spellings","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Traps and checked spellings"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A plain spelling traps when its precondition fails, like an "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Array"},{"type":"text","text":" subscript out of range: it is"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"the fast path, for callers who know the precondition holds. Beside it, a "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"checked:"},{"type":"text","text":" spelling"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"throws a typed error instead, one of those in "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/collectionerrors"},{"type":"text","text":"; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"try?"},{"type":"text","text":" turns it into an"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"optional."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["let primes: AVLTree = [2, 3, 5, 7]","primes[2]                    \/\/ 5","try primes[checked: 9]       \/\/ throws IndexOutOfRange"]},{"inlineContent":[{"text":"A mutation that would break a structure’s invariant, such as joining two treaps whose elements","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"interleave, throws on its plain spelling and changes nothing. Where the standard library’s","type":"text"},{"text":" ","type":"text"},{"text":"collections return an optional (","type":"text"},{"code":"remove(_:)","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":", a dictionary’s subscript, ","type":"text"},{"code":"min()","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":"), these do too.","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Grafluent-conversions","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Grafluent conversions"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"A collection whose shape is a tree converts to the Grafluent type of that shape: "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"BinaryTree"},{"type":"text","text":","},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"Arborescence"},{"type":"text","text":", "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"RootedTree"},{"type":"text","text":" or "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"PrefixTree"},{"type":"text","text":", with an initializer on the Grafluent type that"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"costs O("},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") once. Structures whose shape is a general graph, such as decision diagrams and"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"automata, offer a view that is a Grafluent graph without copying. Either way, Grafluent’s"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"algorithms, drawings and file formats run over the collection; its own operations never go"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"through the conversion. "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"doc:\/\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/GrafluentCollections\/SeeingACollectionAsAGraph"},{"type":"text","text":" shows the round trip."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"anchor":"Modules","level":3,"type":"heading","text":"Modules"},{"rows":[[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Group"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Modules","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Search trees"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/binarysearchtrees","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (AVL, red–black and splay trees, treaps), "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/btrees","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (B-trees), "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/skiplists","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (skip lists)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Tries"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/tries","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (tries over any sequence of symbols, radix and Patricia trees, Aho–Corasick automata)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Suffix structures"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/suffixstructures","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (suffix arrays with LCP, suffix trees, suffix automata)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Decision diagrams"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/decisiondiagrams","type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" (reduced ordered BDDs, zero-suppressed ZDDs)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Range and spatial trees"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/rangetrees"},{"type":"text","text":" (Fenwick trees, segment trees with lazy propagation, interval trees), "},{"type":"reference","isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/spatialtrees"},{"type":"text","text":" (k-d trees, quadtrees, octrees)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"text":"Sequences and persistence","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/ropes","type":"reference"},{"text":" (ropes: sequences as balanced trees of chunks), ","type":"text"},{"isActive":true,"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/persistenttrees","type":"reference"},{"text":" (path-copying weight-balanced trees that keep every version)","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Caches"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"reference","identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/caches","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":" (LRU caches)"}],"type":"paragraph"}]],[[{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"Shared"}],"type":"paragraph"}],[{"inlineContent":[{"identifier":"https:\/\/tyler-keith-thompson.github.io\/GrafluentCollections\/documentation\/collectionerrors","overridingTitle":"CollectionErrors","overridingTitleInlineContent":[{"code":"CollectionErrors","type":"codeVoice"}],"isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"text":": the errors the ","type":"text"},{"code":"checked:","type":"codeVoice"},{"text":" spellings throw, re-exported by every module that throws them","type":"text"}],"type":"paragraph"}]]],"type":"table","header":"row"}],"kind":"content"}],"abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"Graph-shaped collections for Swift: search trees, tries, suffix structures, decision diagrams,"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"range and spatial trees, ropes, persistent trees and caches, with value semantics, built on"},{"type":"t